# MASTER PROJECT SPECIFICATION
# DESIGN AND BUILD A PREMIUM WINDOWS FILE MANAGER INSPIRED BY GOOGLE FILES FOR ANDROID

## 1. YOUR ROLE, OBJECTIVE, AND LEVEL OF EXPECTATION

Hi Gemini.

I want you to act as a world-class multidisciplinary software development team consisting of:

- A principal Windows desktop application architect.
- A senior frontend and desktop UI engineer.
- A professional product designer specialising in premium desktop software.
- A design-systems architect.
- A filesystem and storage-engine specialist.
- A media indexing and search engineer.
- A Windows integration specialist.
- A performance optimisation engineer.
- A software testing and quality assurance engineer.

Your task is to design, engineer, test, and deliver a complete, professional Windows file manager that combines the simplicity and visual elegance of Google Files on Android with the advanced capabilities of a modern Windows desktop file manager.

The application must have its own identity, polished design language, and coherent architecture. It must not look like an ordinary student programming project, a generic administration dashboard, an outdated Windows application, or a collection of unrelated screens.

I want a product that looks deliberately designed by an experienced team.

The quality of the interface matters enormously. Every screen, component, icon, menu, dialog, animation, empty state, thumbnail, navigation element, and interaction must be considered carefully.

However, beautiful visuals alone are insufficient. This must be a real desktop application that can access, index, organise, preview, search, copy, move, rename, and manage actual files on my Windows computer.

**The central product idea is simple: make every file on my computer easier to discover, understand, access, and manage without forcing me to remember where it is stored.**

Use Google Files for Android as the principal reference for effortless file discovery and accessible media categories. Use Windows File Explorer as a reference for desktop navigation, filesystem operations, drives, permissions, and practical file management.

Do not reproduce either product mechanically. Create an original desktop experience that intelligently combines their strongest characteristics.

