### Section 5: Suggested files

If enabled, suggest files based on recent activity or frequently visited locations.

Explain why a suggestion appears when appropriate.

Allow suggestions to be disabled.

Do not upload file names, file contents, or usage histories to an external service.

### Section 6: Indexing status

When a scan is in progress, show a restrained status indicator with:

- Current scan status.
- Number of files discovered, when available.
- Locations being processed.
- Pause or cancel controls where supported.
- An option to open indexing settings.

Do not block normal file browsing while indexing runs.

### Empty home state

If no locations have been indexed, show a professionally designed onboarding screen with a clear explanation and an action to select folders.

Do not display fabricated file counts or fake recent files.

